WEBVTT

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:09.980
<b>Let's guess what date
 the target, Lupin III, will die</b>

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:16.490
<b>All winning bids will share 
a pot of 50 mill in Bitmoney</b>

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:22.500
<b>When do <i>you</i> think Lupin III will die?</b>

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:27.910
I've got a present for you, Lupin.

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:30.290
Your first one from me in four years.

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:36.110
If anyone's gonna kill you, 
it should be me.

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:03.970
<b>Zenigata's Pride and the Desert Dust</b>

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:11.310
<b>Who's the babe?</b>

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:11.310
<b>Time for a plot twist!</b>

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:11.310
<b>She's smokin' hot!!!!</b>

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:11.310
<b>Lupin's really screwed now</b>

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:11.310
<b>And in walks the ex!</b>

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:12.060
<b>Wow, she's beautiful!!</b>

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:12.860
<b>Who is she?</b>

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:13.480
<b>All hell's about to break loose</b>

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:16.790
Ready to receive your final present?

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:18.380
Nah, I think I'll pass.

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:19.910
Go and return it.

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:23.800
I wouldn't bother reaching for whatever 
you've got in your hairpiece.

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:28.870
I'll count down to your gift, Lupin.

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:37.800
Lupin!

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:39.340
Zenigata?!

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:40.380
Pops?!

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:42.770
Get in! You, too, young lady!

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:43.930
<b>That was sudden</b>

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:43.930
<b>Whoa now</b>

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:43.930
<b>Just when things were getting good~</b>

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:43.930
<b>From outta nowhere?</b>

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:43.930
<b>Who??</b>

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:43.930
<b>What the bejesus?!</b>

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:44.680
<b>Way to spoil the mood</b>

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:45.430
<b>That's Inspector Zenigata. 
He's ICPO.</b>

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:46.180
<b>Who's this dweeb?</b>

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:47.270
<b>What the hell?</b>

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:49.890
Let's go, Amy.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:51.140
Lupin!

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:00.230
Pops, not that I don't 
appreciate the sweet rescue,

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:02.740
but you know you can't 
arrest me here, right?

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:03.890
I realize that!

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:07.570
So I'm taking you across the border, 
where I <i>can</i> arrest you!

00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:09.450
Gotta love that work ethic...

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:20.600
You just had to get in the way, 
didn't you, Zenigata?

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:24.150
Nice to see you again, Jigen.

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:28.120
Didn't figure you'd show up to
try and cash in on Lupin, too.

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:31.480
Something wrong with that?

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:34.470
Women can be damn scary.

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:37.970
You think so? I can think 
of something even scarier.

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:39.290
And what's that?

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:42.780
Men who are staunchly
 loyal to their friends.

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:54.360
Even Fujiko's after you now.

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:55.770
Was that a lover's tiff?

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:58.120
Not at all.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:00.380
There's nothing between me and her now.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:04.630
After you used to go around, drooling 
over her, and calling her "Fujicakes"?

00:04:04.630 --> 00:04:06.550
That's ancient history.

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:09.630
All she is to me now is a competitor in 
this biz, and a dangerous one at that.

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:16.390
The Bwandan military?

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:19.980
I'm Zenigata with the ICPO!

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:22.150
I want to speak to your commanding officer!

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:24.250
What in the world?!

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:27.480
I wouldn't bother, Pops!

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:30.780
The guys who run this country are 
practically mobsters themselves.

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:34.160
Damn it all! No wonder they 
don't want ICPO membership!

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:44.890
Chasing a bounty like this...

00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:47.230
As a fellow public servant, I'm outraged!

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:51.390
Get ready to jump clear.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:10.330
<b>Now it's getting good! LOL</b>

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:10.330
<b>I thought he was a goner, for sure</b>

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:10.330
<b>Lupin sure is hard to kill~</b>

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:10.330
<b>What the hell? Lupin's not dead</b>

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:10.330
<b>And the game continues</b>

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:11.660
<b>Who cares? It's entertaining</b>

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:13.650
Nice try, Lupin.

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:17.780
But the bounty on the assassination site 
doesn't expire till you're six feet under.

00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:20.430
We'll never run out of hitmen.

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:23.920
<b>I've confirmed that new killers 
have entered the country</b>

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:26.800
<b>He can either stay there and die,</b>

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:29.260
<b>or cross the border and 
get nailed by the pigs.</b>

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:30.930
<b>Either way, Lupin's done for.</b>

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:38.930
I guess we've finally shaken our pursuers.

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:42.340
Can't be easy to spot us here in the bush.

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:44.050
There are no paths in here, though.

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:47.170
No need to fret, miss.

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:48.450
Look there!

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:51.590
In the southern hemisphere, 
the sun travels in a northern arc!

00:05:51.590 --> 00:05:54.450
Which means walking in the opposite 
direction will take us south!

00:05:55.460 --> 00:05:57.330
Hello, Underworld.

00:05:57.330 --> 00:05:58.950
Connect using the Ponion proxy.

00:05:59.470 --> 00:06:01.490
What's the shortest route to the border?

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:06.440
This is a AR Map created by
 a company called Shake Hands.

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:10.170
Gotta love all these
 modern conveniences, huh?

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:17.480
By the way, if you're 
looking for potable water...

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:21.890
What's the meaning of this?

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:25.840
For the ICPO to be seen 
aiding a wanted criminal...

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:28.740
Not to mention, it was broadcast globally.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:30.130
This is bad.

00:06:30.130 --> 00:06:33.530
All Inspector Zenigata has 
done is apprehend a criminal.

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:36.140
The public won't see it that way.

00:06:36.140 --> 00:06:39.540
We'll have to open disciplinary 
proceedings when he gets back.

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:41.650
We must keep up appearances.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:47.300
Run an object search.

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:50.240
Cross-reference with edible flora.

00:06:54.230 --> 00:06:56.430
Well, look at you, Little Miss Botany.

00:06:56.790 --> 00:07:00.590
Anyone with an internet 
connection can be a scientist.

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:02.640
As long as you know what to search for.

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:12.040
So you were a shut-in for 15 years?

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:13.850
I wasn't a shut-in.

00:07:13.850 --> 00:07:15.930
I just had no reason to go outside.

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:19.090
So what's your take on the outside world?

00:07:19.090 --> 00:07:19.950
It's inconvenient.

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:22.020
Communication takes too long.

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:23.430
That's what bothers you?

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:25.540
There are countless threats to your life,

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:27.840
it's hot, and it's dirty.

00:07:28.690 --> 00:07:29.960
The food's bad, too.

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:32.750
That's because you're with this guy!

00:07:34.060 --> 00:07:37.260
Miss, you should be attending school.

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:40.170
Don't worry your pretty little head. 
This matter with Marco Polo...

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:43.390
will all go away once we've got you into 
the ICPO's witness protection program.

00:07:43.390 --> 00:07:45.750
We'll keep you safe and sound!

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:48.940
I see no reason to go to school.

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:53.000
I can find any information 
I want on the internet,

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:55.350
and when it comes to basic logic 
exercises, like math problems,

00:07:55.350 --> 00:07:57.250
I'm confident that I'm 
already above average.

00:07:57.250 --> 00:07:58.400
I bet.

00:07:58.400 --> 00:07:59.950
But you can make friends there.

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:02.260
I have plenty of friends on the internet.

00:08:02.780 --> 00:08:04.600
From all over the world.

00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:07.630
Where gender, age and race don't matter.

00:08:07.990 --> 00:08:13.160
I can't imagine a space as confined as a school 
offering even a fraction of that diversity.

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:14.630
Well, now!

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:16.960
You've got the wrong end of the stick, miss.

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:20.010
Love and friendship aren't things you 
can measure in purely logical terms.

00:08:20.010 --> 00:08:22.590
Do you consider Lupin a friend?

00:08:23.470 --> 00:08:27.640
Have your irrational actions to help us
 been your idea of friendship?

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:29.130
Hmph. Of course not!

00:08:29.130 --> 00:08:32.150
How could I ever be friends with a lying, 
law-breaking, womanizing scoundrel?!

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:34.890
Okay, now tell me how you <i>really </i>feel...

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:37.410
Oh, I get it.

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:38.390
You do?

00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:44.400
Don't worry. I believe that 
all forms of love are valid.

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:50.630
You've got it all wrong! I only came 
out here because Lupin was...

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:51.420
Well, y'know...

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:55.680
Two lovers on opposite sides of the law... 
Sounds like something out of a story.

00:08:56.670 --> 00:08:57.790
That's not it at all!

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:03.060
I love ya, Pops!

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:05.240
Shut your trap, you monkey-faced idiot!

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:08.820
Forgive me, darling! 
I never realized you had feelings for me!

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:10.810
I <i>will</i> shoot you, I swear!

00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:12.550
Don't wave that scary 
thing around like that!

00:09:12.550 --> 00:09:15.180
But if you wanna point your <i>other </i>piece 
at me... The one in your pants...

00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:17.230
What are you even saying, you imbecile?!

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:17.830
They're certainly enjoying themselves...

00:09:17.230 --> 00:09:18.190
Ooh, such thick sideburns...

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:20.820
Enough! Stop now!

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:23.160
You'll pay for this, Lupin!

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:29.780
It's going to be all desert for a while.

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:33.020
If we make a beeline for 
the border, it's a 50 km trek.

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:35.200
The temperature at this time 
of year is around 40°C...

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:36.610
We should be able to walk it.

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:40.430
Isn't this your first time in a desert?

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:43.420
I've got a good idea of the broader picture.

00:09:43.420 --> 00:09:47.150
I've read the equivalent of 83 books
 on desert environments.

00:09:47.590 --> 00:09:49.530
Well, aren't you studious?

00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:51.460
Only the abridged versions, though.

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:53.330
The kind compiled when an AI summarizes...

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:55.200
the most important parts 
through machine learning.

00:10:08.990 --> 00:10:16.600
<i>After wandering through the desert for a day, 
it was like I was on a different planet.</i>

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:20.550
<i>In time, I felt I had stopped 
being an Earthling altogether,</i>

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:22.280
<i>and was now a denizen of a desert world,</i>

00:10:22.280 --> 00:10:25.320
<i>and the intense sun began to feel 
pleasant on my skin instead of—</i>

00:10:24.550 --> 00:10:25.580
Stop!

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:29.370
You done already? What about your 84th book?

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:32.060
It's fiction. I wanted non-fiction.

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:34.280
And there's nothing pleasant 
about this situation.

00:10:34.910 --> 00:10:37.350
Well, it takes all sorts.

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:41.830
Maybe the guy who wrote it was a masochist.

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:46.710
What would you write about the desert, then?

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:49.880
It's the worst!

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:51.500
Absolute garbage! A wasteland!

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:54.540
Just a blinding, bone-dry hellhole!

00:11:07.940 --> 00:11:12.920
Maybe we... should've 
waited... for nightfall...

00:11:12.920 --> 00:11:16.530
This is still better than the
military catching up with us.

00:11:22.810 --> 00:11:23.870
Amy!

00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:43.830
If anything happens to me...

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:45.920
...can you look after the girl?

00:11:46.230 --> 00:11:48.910
I refuse to believe anything 
<i>could</i> happen to you.

00:11:49.380 --> 00:11:50.820
But consider it done.

00:11:53.370 --> 00:11:55.810
I appreciate it, Pops.

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:00.150
<b>Imagine if they just died in the desert</b>

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:00.150
<b>There's no way they're stupid 
enough to go into the desert lol</b>

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:00.150
<b>This is gonna stay boring 
if they can't find them</b>

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:00.150
<b>Haven't they found Lupin yet?</b>

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:00.150
<b>They probably went into the desert</b>

00:12:00.150 --> 00:12:01.740
<b>No way. It's practically suicide</b>

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:04.990
<b>I guess even Drone Fighter 
can't find them now</b>

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:07.280
<b>Yeah, and he's at the 
top of the rankings</b>

00:12:08.630 --> 00:12:10.800
You've gotta be kidding me, Lupin.

00:12:10.800 --> 00:12:13.780
You think you can just wander off 
and die where no one can see?

00:12:13.780 --> 00:12:16.510
What fun would that be?

00:12:27.190 --> 00:12:29.730
Look, Lupin, a camel!

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:32.850
You've got it all wrong, Pops...

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:36.230
It's a bunch of beautiful dark-skinned babes!

00:12:40.810 --> 00:12:42.770
You awake now, Amy?

00:12:43.180 --> 00:12:46.830
The sun's almost down... 
It'll cool down.

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:50.330
Windmill? That means...

00:12:51.060 --> 00:12:52.560
...water!

00:12:52.560 --> 00:12:54.000
Quit squirming!

00:12:58.440 --> 00:12:59.450
Water...

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:02.360
Water. Water!

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:53.790
Don't gulp it down so fast.

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:55.940
The cold water will upset your stomach.

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:14.650
Once we're through this bit, 
we'll be at the border.

00:14:14.650 --> 00:14:17.860
And you finally get to arrest me, huh?

00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:21.990
Lupin. Come peacefully.

00:14:21.990 --> 00:14:25.280
Your face is comical enough 
without the need for jokes, Pops.

00:14:25.280 --> 00:14:28.870
Once you're in custody, these assassins 
will have a harder time getting to you!

00:14:30.440 --> 00:14:33.180
Thanks, Pops. But y'know...

00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:37.700
I wouldn't be Lupin if I did that.

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:43.940
<b>There, there!</b>

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:43.940
<b>Looks like they didn't get away~</b>

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:43.940
<b>Drone Fighter rules!!!!!</b>

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:43.940
<b>Found ya, found ya, found ya</b>

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:43.940
<b>There!</b>

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:43.940
<b>GJ Drone Fighter</b>

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:43.940
<b>Don't let them escape!</b>

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:44.650
<b>It's Lupin!!</b>

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:45.530
<b>Good job finding 'em</b>

00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:46.480
<b>Drone Fighter is GOAT</b>

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:47.860
<b>They're nearly at the border</b>

00:14:47.860 --> 00:14:49.280
<b>Hey, hitgoons, Lupin's 
almost in the clear!</b>

00:14:54.190 --> 00:14:56.700
Take care of it before 
they cross the border.

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:59.360
If you take out Lupin, I'll give 
you a portion of the winnings.

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:01.190
Leave it to us, sir!

00:15:01.190 --> 00:15:03.370
There's nowhere to hide in the desert.

00:15:03.370 --> 00:15:05.200
That money's as good as ours!

00:15:10.700 --> 00:15:12.210
And here they come.

00:15:12.210 --> 00:15:13.350
Get in position!

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:17.960
It's the same helicopter as last time...

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:21.720
But this time, it's carrying missiles!

00:15:23.460 --> 00:15:24.730
What?!

00:15:31.730 --> 00:15:33.610
Lupin! Zenigata!

00:15:33.970 --> 00:15:35.150
Did that get them?

00:15:35.150 --> 00:15:36.620
There's still one more target!

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:39.180
Lupin! Zenigata!

00:15:45.810 --> 00:15:48.520
Hunting people is more exciting 
than I thought it would be.

00:15:49.820 --> 00:15:52.020
Cowards! Shooting at us like that!

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:54.760
Amy!

00:15:56.510 --> 00:15:58.900
Stop playing. Time you finished the job.

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:00.510
If you insist.

00:16:21.020 --> 00:16:22.020
What?!

00:16:22.760 --> 00:16:25.010
Oh, no! The rotors!

00:16:34.520 --> 00:16:35.710
She did it!

00:16:35.710 --> 00:16:37.600
Amy! You okay?!

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:15.040
I'm alive.

00:17:41.720 --> 00:17:44.600
Look. That fence marks the border.

00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:48.120
Once we're past that, I guess we're 
back to playing hide and seek.

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:50.090
Inspector Zenigata!

00:17:53.980 --> 00:17:57.000
Well, since you're offering, 
I'll bum a ride to the next town.

00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:58.750
I've got the girl with me, after all.

00:17:58.750 --> 00:17:59.960
No need to cut our journey short.

00:17:59.960 --> 00:18:02.590
I can give you a lift all 
the way to a prison cell.

00:18:04.090 --> 00:18:06.860
Oh, I couldn't possibly impose!

00:18:10.030 --> 00:18:10.690
Get down!

00:18:12.510 --> 00:18:13.480
A sniper?

00:18:13.480 --> 00:18:15.800
An ambush? All the way out here?

00:18:15.800 --> 00:18:17.600
Pops, keep Amy safe.

00:18:21.440 --> 00:18:22.390
Lupin!

00:18:22.390 --> 00:18:24.220
Get going! I'll catch up!

00:18:24.220 --> 00:18:28.300
We need to go. He won't try 
and escape until you're safe.

00:18:28.300 --> 00:18:29.950
Is he an idiot?

00:18:29.950 --> 00:18:31.380
You mean you didn't know?

00:18:31.380 --> 00:18:34.620
In my country, "Lupin" is 
synonymous with "idiot."

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:39.680
